# RJR site: rules for AI edits

## Workflow
- Edit `content.py` (words/data), `build.py` (templates), `static/assets/site.css` (styles). Never edit `site/`; it is regenerated by `python3 build.py`.
- After any change run `python3 build.py` and check the output builds cleanly.
- Keep `build.py` compatible with Python 3.8+: no nested same-type quotes inside f-strings; prefer `%` formatting as the file does.
- Internal URLs in templates are written root-relative (`/services/...`); `relativise()` converts them per page. Don't hard-code `../`.

## Content
- Only facts supplied by the business. Never invent prices, response times, 24/7 claims, guarantees, accreditations, insurance, job counts, staff names beyond "Ryan" (from reviews), or reviews.
- Reviews and QUOTES are verbatim: do not correct spelling or trim mid-sentence.
- Before/after pairs in PROJECTS are verified (same building). Don't re-pair or relabel photos.
- Answer-first copy: the first paragraph of a page or FAQ answers the question directly.
- British English. Hedge legal/planning guidance ("may need consent", "check with the council").

## Design system (brutalist, typography-first)
- Colours: ONLY the brand set from the logo: `--red` (+ `--red-deep` hover, `--red-bright` for red on charcoal, `--red-tint` quiet bands, `--red-line`), `--ink` (charcoal), `--light`/`--light-2` (white), `--grey`. Roles: white = reading, charcoal = structure and dark bands, red = brand, action and markers. White text on red only.
- Never: border-radius, box-shadow, gradients, rounded cards, icon grids, centred hero with two rounded buttons, or a background highlight behind running text (use colour: `.hl`, `.hl-o`).
- Type sizes only via `--step-*` tokens (fluid clamp, 1.250 → 1.333 modular scale). No px font sizes.
- Spacing only via `--s-*` rhythm tokens and `gap`; elements carry no margins.
- Body copy max 65ch. Display type Archivo 800/900 with tight tracking; labels IBM Plex Mono uppercase with +0.08em tracking.
- Layout: asymmetric 12-col grid (`.col-idx` 3 / `.col-main` 9), sections split by rules, left-aligned.
- Band order on pages: hero (photo + charcoal overlay) → white/alt bands → red urgent band → charcoal band → red CTA → charcoal footer. Logo (`static/assets/logo.webp`) in header and footer; never re-type the brand name as the logo.
- Must work at 360px with no horizontal scroll; mobile bar (WhatsApp/Call) is fixed at the bottom.

## Performance
- All images go through `tools/optimise_images.py` (WebP srcset, width/height set, lazy below the fold).
- No new JS libraries. The only scripts are `consent.js` and `quote.js`.
- The quote form must never send data to a server: inputs have no `name` attributes and `quote.js` only builds a wa.me link on the visitor's device. If that ever changes, update the privacy policy in `build_legal`.
